Dual-use functionality disclosure

@liaosiyuan123/dshc is an unofficial terminal frontend for DeepSeek Harness. Its
intended legitimate use is software development inside repositories selected by
the operator. Through the upstream Harness runtime it can inspect and modify
files, search source code, run shell commands, use skills, and delegate work to
subagents.

Those capabilities can affect the local filesystem and execute programs with
the authority granted to the Harness child process. The shipped configuration
uses the upstream workspace-write sandbox and approval policy, fails closed when
the configured sandbox is unavailable, and does not silently promote itself to
unconfined execution. Operators remain responsible for reviewing requests and
using the package only on systems and repositories they are authorized to
access.

The project is not designed for credential theft, unauthorized access,
persistence, exploitation, evasion, or destructive activity. Security issues
should be reported according to SECURITY.md without posting real secrets or
private repository content in public issues.
